  message: "Data-gap collection for WI-nigah Tier 3 prioritization (2026-05-31, post-WI-kaziv close): ran hypergumbo on a 6-repo per-language cohort. Per-analyzer unresolved external-target call-edge volume (all 0% dst_ref, confirming retrofit gap): lua/kong=6893, d_lang/dmd=1121, tcl/redis=403, pascal/sherpa-onnx=73, groovy/spring-boot=41, objc/feyncalc=0. The 0/13 totals for objc on feyncalc is a cohort failure — feyncalc .m files are Mathematica not Objective-C. Languages with no representative repo in the prospector pool (cobol, fennel, gdscript, gleam, janet, nim, odin, pony, solidity) or with the only candidate repo being prohibitively large (perl/powershell/asm in virtualbox, ada/fish/haxe/v_lang with too few files): no data collected. Data-driven Tier 3 prioritization for WI-nigah residual scope: HIGH-VOLUME RETROFIT TARGETS lua (6.9K unresolved) > d_lang > tcl; LOW-VOLUME OR INSUFFICIENT DATA pascal/groovy/objc + the no-data set. Full per-repo numbers and hg.json artifacts at /tmp/wi-nigah-data/. This closes the data gap that the WI-kaziv discussion called out and feeds the WI-nigah todo_soft conversion."  # c7ef
